WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.690
Thieves stole card details from
customers of a large US retailer.

2
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.670
To do it, they had to reach
the store's card tills,

3
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.290
where customers pay.

4
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.870
But their route started somewhere strange:

5
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.150
a firm that fixes heating
and air-conditioning.

6
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.390
Air-con on one side,
card tills on the other.

7
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.510
How could one route link them?

8
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:24.890
In this mission, you'll see how authentication
checks that users really are who

9
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:26.270
they claim to be.

10
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:30.930
You'll find out why each person should
get only the access their role needs.

11
00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:35.810
And you'll meet firewalls, which allow
or block traffic using a set of security

12
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:36.830
rules.

13
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.680
Your mission: work out how the thieves
got from the air-con firm to the tills.
